{"files":[{"content":"#include<stdio.h>\n#include<stdlib.h>\n#include<string.h>\n\n/* Maximum size (in char) for neighbors and compute lists */\n#define MAX 100\n\ntypedef struct {\n  int id;\n  float value;\n  char neighbors[MAX];\n} Node;\n\ntypedef struct {\n  float value;\n  unsigned char ready;\n} CostEntry;\n\n/* Reads input, allocates memory, writes graph size and node list. Returns the graph. */\nNode* read_input(char* fname, int *n, char* list) {\n  Node* data = NULL;\n  FILE *fl = NULL;\n\n  if (fname == NULL)\n    fl = stdin;\n  else\n    fl = fopen(fname, \"r\");\n\n  if (fl == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  // header\n  fscanf(fl, \"%d %[^\\n]\", n, list);\n\n  if (*n > 0) {\n    data = (Node*) malloc ((*n)*sizeof(Node));\n    if(data == NULL){\n      fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n      exit(1);\n    }\n  }\n\n  for(int i = 0; i < *n; i++)\n    fscanf(fl, \"%d %f %[^\\n]\", &data[i].id, &data[i].value, data[i].neighbors);\n\n  fclose(fl);\n  return data;\n}\n\n/* Returns the first index of the node with the given id or -1 if not found */\nint find_by_id(const int ids[], int id, int size){\n  int i = 0;\n\n  while((i < size) && ids[i] != id)\n    i++;\n\n  if(i < size)\n    return i;\n\n  return -1;\n}\n\n/* Computes and caches the sum for the node with the given id */\nfloat get_costly(Node *g, const int ids[], int id, int size, CostEntry *cache) {\n  int nd = find_by_id(ids, id, size);\n  if(nd < 0)\n    return 0;\n\n  if(cache[nd].ready)\n    return cache[nd].value;\n\n  int idmax = -1;\n  float max = 0;\n  char aux[MAX];\n  char *auxptr;\n  strcpy(aux, g[nd].neighbors);\n  char *t = strtok_r(aux, \" \", &auxptr);\n\n  while(t != NULL) {\n    int neighbor_id = atoi(t);\n    int d = find_by_id(ids, neighbor_id, size);\n    if (d >= 0 && max < g[d].value) {\n      max = g[d].value;\n      idmax = neighbor_id;\n    }\n    t = strtok_r(NULL, \" \", &auxptr);\n  }\n\n  float r = g[nd].value;\n  if(idmax != -1)\n    r += get_costly(g, ids, idmax, size, cache);\n\n  cache[nd].value = r;\n  cache[nd].ready = 1;\n  return r;\n}\n\n/* Main program - calls read input, computes sum for each node in the list, prints output */\nint main() {\n  char *fileN = NULL;\n  char computelist[MAX];\n  int n = -1;\n  Node* input = NULL;\n\n  input = read_input(fileN, &n, computelist);\n\n  CostEntry *cache = (CostEntry*) calloc(n > 0 ? n : 1, sizeof(CostEntry));\n  if(cache == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    free(input);\n    exit(1);\n  }\n\n  /* Keep IDs contiguous so lookups scan a compact array instead of striding\n     through the larger Node records. */\n  int *ids = (int*) malloc((n > 0 ? n : 1) * sizeof(int));\n  if(ids == NULL) {\n    fprintf(stderr, \"Error!\\n\");\n    free(cache);\n    free(input);\n    exit(1);\n  }\n  for(int i = 0; i < n; i++)\n    ids[i] = input[i].id;\n\n  // process\n  for(char *c = strtok(computelist, \" \"); c != NULL; c = strtok(NULL, \" \"))\n    printf(\"%s: %f\\n\", c, get_costly(input, ids, atoi(c), n, cache));\n\n  free(ids);\n  free(cache);\n  free(input);\n  return 0;\n}\n","path":"src/graph.c"}],"hypothesis":"A compact contiguous sidecar of node IDs should reduce cache-line traffic during repeated linear ID lookups compared with scanning the ID field at the larger stride of each Node record, while preserving lookup order and computation behavior.","notes":"Retains the existing per-node cost cache, neighbor-selection order, and accumulation order. Correctness and performance evaluation are delegated to the controller.","research":{"queries":[],"urls":[]},"sources_kept":[],"transformations":["Build a contiguous ID array once after input parsing and use it for the existing first-match linear lookup, preserving node order and duplicate-ID behavior.","Pass the ID sidecar through recursive cost evaluation and release it with the existing allocations." ]}